WEBVTT


00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.500
Is Microsoft Fabric just a new Power BI?

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:07.101
Absolutely not. This is fabric and this is Power BI.

00:00:07.102 --> 00:00:08.581
Power BI is a reporting tool

00:00:08.582 --> 00:00:11.541
and reporting is usually the last step in a data life cycle.

00:00:11.542 --> 00:00:14.681
Before that your data goes through multiple tools.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.340
Some tools bring data in like Data Factory and 5 grand.

00:00:18.341 --> 00:00:20.501
Some store it like snowflakes and sign UPS.

00:00:20.502 --> 00:00:24.041
Then there are tools that transform it like data bricks and DBT.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.700
Then comes your reporting with tools like Power BI and Tableau.

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:30.741
And now we also have AI tools like punditry and lagnograph.

00:00:30.742 --> 00:00:31.621
So as you can see,

00:00:31.622 --> 00:00:34.941
Power BI is just one of the tools in the whole life cycle.

00:00:34.942 --> 00:00:36.221
Fabric is Microsoft saying

00:00:36.222 --> 00:00:38.661
what if all of this could be done in one platform?

00:00:38.662 --> 00:00:41.441
So instead of jumping between four or five tools,

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.500
we have one place where raw data gets converted into insights

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:49.001
and can be used for AI within one system itself.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.780
And if you are a Power BI developer,

00:00:50.781 --> 00:00:52.741
fabric expands what you can do

00:00:52.742 --> 00:00:54.941
because now you're not just building reports,

00:00:54.942 --> 00:00:57.581
you can now understand and control where your data comes from,

00:00:57.582 --> 00:00:59.641
how it's stored, how it's shaped

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.660
and you can build AI agents on top of it all,

00:01:02.661 --> 00:01:06.181
essentially making you the owner of entire data life cycle.

00:01:06.182 --> 00:01:09.828
And that is what full stack data professionals do.
